Work from the latest main branch of hiyroscript/alva.

Implement three related changes:

1. Fix #0001’s Mid-Air Dodge artwork facing the opposite direction from the fighter.
2. Add #0001’s new Throw animation on the existing internal primary action.
3. Add #0001’s animated shuriken projectile, including real projectile movement, collision, damage and rendering.

Preserve the existing Charge, Defense/Dodge, BA1, BA2, Energy, physics, HUD, and training-CPU behavior.

Do not redesign unrelated systems.

1. Current relevant architecture

The current game already has:

* generic primary, special, action1, action2 combat inputs
* primary on keyboard J
* primary on gamepad X / Square
* a reserved Primary touch button in the upper-right action cluster
* BA1 on action1
* BA2 on action2
* Defense on defense
* #0001 ground Dodge and Mid-Air Dodge
* a generic attack definition/combat system
* no projectile subsystem
* fighter rendering through Battle.drawFighter()
* one global character sourceFacing

Character #0001 currently defines:

sourceFacing: 1

meaning its normal source art is assumed to face right.

Battle.drawFighter() currently determines mirroring approximately as:

const flip = f.facing !== (f.def.sourceFacing || 1);

That global assumption is the cause of the Mid-Air Dodge facing bug.

2. Fix Mid-Air Dodge source orientation

The Mid-Air Dodge artwork is drawn facing the opposite direction from #0001’s normal source art.

Do not fix this by:

* changing fighter.facing
* negating movement
* swapping left/right controls
* globally setting sourceFacing: -1
* horizontally modifying the PNG files
* special-casing midairDodge by name inside Battle.drawFighter()

The fighter’s logical facing is already correct.

This is an art-source orientation problem.

