4. Preserve the metadata through SpriteSet

SpriteSet.build() currently keeps fields such as:

fps
loop
heightRatio
minSpeedScale

Add the animation’s optional source orientation:

sourceFacing: anim.sourceFacing ?? def.sourceFacing ?? 1

or equivalent.

The normalized animation stored in:

set.animations[key]

must know the orientation of its own original artwork.

Do not put orientation on every individual frame unless necessary; it is animation-level metadata.

5. Use current animation orientation when rendering

Change Battle.drawFighter() from the global-only rule to the currently playing animation.

Conceptually:

const sourceFacing =
  f.animator.anim?.sourceFacing ??
  f.def.sourceFacing ??
  1;
const flip = f.facing !== sourceFacing;

Then call drawFrame() normally.

Required result:

Normal right-facing source animation

fighter faces right → no flip
fighter faces left  → flip

Mid-Air Dodge, whose source art faces left

fighter faces right → flip
fighter faces left  → no flip

Do not change the fighter’s actual facing property to achieve this.

