* it travels outside the stage bounds with a small margin
* it hits genuinely solid stage geometry if projectile/solid collision is implemented

Do not let missed projectiles remain forever.

One-way platforms do not need to stop shurikens unless the existing stage collision design makes that clearly desirable.

Do not invent ricochets.

